  "description": "## Task\n\nA librarian walks along a shelf of books, each worth some points. She may take any books she likes, except that she never takes two books that sit side by side (they would make noise together). Find the largest total value she can collect.\n\n## Input\n\n- `values` — a list of non-negative integers, one per book, in shelf order. It may be empty.\n\n## Output\n\nThe maximum total value of a set of books with no two adjacent. An empty shelf gives 0.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\nquiet_shelf_picks([3, 2, 7, 10])  # returns 13\nquiet_shelf_picks([5, 5, 10, 100, 10, 5])  # returns 110\nquiet_shelf_picks([])  # returns 0\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 0 ≤ length of `values` ≤ 10^4\n- 0 ≤ each value ≤ 10^6\n",
